WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.165
"Zing!" Zann exclaimed. "You oversized swamp rat! I'll get you for that."

2
00:00:08.166 --> 00:00:10.915
Picking up a rock, he tossed it at the dragon.

3
00:00:10.916 --> 00:00:13.848
Zing ducked the rock, chattering in annoyance.

4
00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:19.822
Zann grinned. "What do you expect?" he said. "You just tried to roast me!"

5
00:00:19.823 --> 00:00:25.280
The dragon hopped down from the roof, not bothering to unfurl its leathery wings.

6
00:00:25.281 --> 00:00:30.079
It landed beside Zann with a thump. He bent to scratch its pointy little head.

7
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.947
"Did you eat yet?" he asked. "Let's go inside.

8
00:00:33.948 --> 00:00:38.356
I'll conjure up some food for you as soon as I tell Boz about the warning."

9
00:00:38.357 --> 00:00:46.290
The dragon chirped agreeably. Many people kept dragons as pets, but fire whistlers like Zing weren’t very popular.

10
00:00:46.291 --> 00:00:51.536
The breed was too active, too independent, and a little too unpredictable.

11
00:00:51.537 --> 00:00:55.788
Besides, most people didn't like dealing with a pet that could set you on fire.

12
00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:59.567
But Zing was perfect for Zann. They spent hours together.

13
00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:03.072
Their favorite game was to lie in wait and attack each other.

14
00:01:03.073 --> 00:01:07.988
Zann reached for his schoolbag, which he'd dropped during Zing's surprise attack.

15
00:01:07.989 --> 00:01:12.592
"You'd better sleep with one eye open," he told the dragon jokingly.

16
00:01:12.593 --> 00:01:17.588
Dragons couldn't talk, but the smarter ones could understand some human speech.

17
00:01:17.589 --> 00:01:23.731
"Because when you least expect it, I'm going to grab you and feed you to the water blobs."

18
00:01:23.732 --> 00:01:28.955
Zing hissed playfully, sending out a spurt of flame that Zann dodged easily.

19
00:01:28.956 --> 00:01:32.640
He laughed, glancing around for another rock.

20
00:01:32.641 --> 00:01:35.640
Before he could find one, the door flew open.

21
00:01:35.641 --> 00:01:43.443
"Get in here," Boz ordered, the tip of his long, pointy nose quivering as it always did when he was worked up about something.

22
00:01:43.444 --> 00:01:51.421
Zann's grandfather was clutching the tattered diary in which he recorded everything important that happened to him. "I need to talk to you."

23
00:01:51.422 --> 00:01:57.087
Zann guessed that Boz had already heard about the message. "I'm coming," he said.

24
00:01:57.088 --> 00:02:00.782
Like the outside, the inside of their house rarely changed.

25
00:02:00.783 --> 00:02:07.344
Half the furniture was boring and utilitarian, transported there by Boz from his old home in First City.

26
00:02:07.345 --> 00:02:13.660
The rest was cool stuff that Zann's parents had conjured, mostly based on interesting things they had seen in their travels:

27
00:02:13.661 --> 00:02:23.002
a statue of a frightening beast from the slopes of Mount Mystery, replicas of the low-slung chairs used by nomadic settlers way out on the Far Frontier,

28
00:02:23.003 --> 00:02:29.086
and an exotic-looking lamp from some other, faraway world. That lamp was Zann's favorite.

29
00:02:29.087 --> 00:02:36.823
He paused beside it, resting a hand on its lumpy surface and glancing at the framed blink images of his family hanging on the walls.

30
00:02:36.824 --> 00:02:41.199
Could his parents be trapped in some mysterious other world even now?

31
00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.287
Could they still be alive despite what most people thought?

32
00:02:44.288 --> 00:02:49.683
Zing scampered over to grab a scorched chew toy. Boz stared at Zann.

33
00:02:49.684 --> 00:02:56.409
His large brown eyes were troubled. "I'm glad you're home," he said, setting his diary on the table.

34
00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.893
"I thought about going down to your school to get you.

35
00:02:59.894 --> 00:03:02.853
Have you heard about the warning from the palace?"

36
00:03:02.854 --> 00:03:08.731
Zann nodded. "An echo crow came to school. The message sounded pretty weird.

37
00:03:08.732 --> 00:03:12.236
Why would Reds suddenly start disappearing?"

38
00:03:12.237 --> 00:03:16.714
"I don't know." Boz rubbed his nose to stop it from quivering.

39
00:03:16.715 --> 00:03:21.210
"I've sent messages to a few friends to see if any of them know anything.

40
00:03:21.211 --> 00:03:27.960
But they haven't responded. That worries me, especially since they're all Reds."

41
00:03:27.961 --> 00:03:32.310
He tapped one finger against another, and several message moths appeared.

42
00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:36.879
Boz focused his gaze on one, muttering a message under his breath.

43
00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:44.226
As he spoke, tiny words etched themselves onto the moth's powdery wings. Zann couldn't help being impressed.

44
00:03:44.227 --> 00:03:47.391
Most people had to inscribe message moths by hand.

45
00:03:47.392 --> 00:03:50.625
Only a few people had the focus to do it by eye.

46
00:03:50.626 --> 00:03:56.897
Sometimes it was easy to forget that his grandfather had been one of the most powerful Magic Masters in the kingdom.

47
00:03:56.898 --> 00:04:02.283
Zann wondered if he himself would ever develop that kind of control over his own powers.

48
00:04:02.284 --> 00:04:06.598
He realized Boz had finished inscribing the message moths and was talking again.

49
00:04:06.599 --> 00:04:09.899
He'd just said something about wanting Zann to stay at home.

50
00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:15.541
"What?" Zann blurted out. "But I told Darb I'd meet him at the swamp after dinner!"

51
00:04:15.542 --> 00:04:20.951
"Sorry, Zann. We need to be careful until I find out what we're dealing with."

52
00:04:20.952 --> 00:04:27.852
Boz waved a hand to send the moths fluttering out the window. "I can't risk you wandering off."

53
00:04:27.853 --> 00:04:33.575
"What's the difference? It's not like anything ever happens way out here in Swamp Bottom.

54
00:04:33.576 --> 00:04:38.856
I still don't know why you decided to move to this place after Mom and Dad disappeared.

55
00:04:38.857 --> 00:04:44.644
We'll never find out what happened to them while we're stuck out here in this boring old backwater."

56
00:04:44.645 --> 00:04:48.197
"I'll make dinner in an hour" was all Boz said.

57
00:04:48.198 --> 00:04:51.131
"You'd better get started on your homework."

58
00:04:51.132 --> 00:04:57.137
"Typical," thought Zann. Boz never wanted to talk about what had happened to Zann's parents.

59
00:04:57.138 --> 00:05:03.669
Zann didn't get it. Didn't Boz want to find them if they were still out there somewhere?

60
00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:08.347
"Come here, Zing," he called. "Dinnertime."

61
00:05:08.348 --> 00:05:11.740
He rubbed his fingers together and pointed at the dragon's food dish.

62
00:05:11.741 --> 00:05:15.498
A big helping of green, slimy dragon mush appeared.

63
00:05:15.499 --> 00:05:21.909
Zing flapped his wings in thanks. Then he shot out a flicker of flame and instantly cooked the mush.

64
00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:25.804
It smelled disgusting, but the dragon slurped it up eagerly.

65
00:05:25.805 --> 00:05:29.208
Zann turned around and realized Boz was watching him.

66
00:05:29.209 --> 00:05:35.872
"I'm not trying to ruin your fun, Zann," Boz said. "I just want to protect you."

67
00:05:35.873 --> 00:05:42.763
"I know." Zann felt guilty for his earlier thoughts. "It's okay."

68
00:05:42.764 --> 00:05:47.562
But after dinner Zann felt much too restless to sit in his room and study.

69
00:05:47.563 --> 00:05:51.636
He checked to make sure Boz wasn't nearby.

70
00:05:51.637 --> 00:05:58.911
Then he rubbed his hands together and zapped himself out of the house.

